abstract: >-
  An Agent Skill for writing, editing and pre-submission auditing of
  scientific and technical texts in Russian, English and Japanese: journal articles,
  reviews, conference theses, extended abstracts, monographs, grant
  applications, research reports, technical documentation, popular-science
  articles, presentations and letters to editors. It drafts from the author's own
  material in the genre's structure without inventing data, verifies claims
  against sources and sources against reality, runs four gates (sources,
  internal facts, provenance and conflicts of interest with the statements the venue
  requires, falsifiability), offers a voice pass that removes bureaucratic
  and template phrasing in the register of the genre, and a language
  check for grammar, spelling and punctuation, with facts frozen,
  scores the text on a venue-calibrated rubric and
  returns an editorial recommendation. Bundled standard-library tools: a
  GOST-aware formatting linter, a version diff for reviewing edits, style
  diagnostics, a genre check and a check for mechanical language slips.
